{
  "correction_rules": [
    "When sentiment history includes a positive sentiment (≥ 0.50), model tends to overestimate prices; reduce forecast by 5-10% in such cases.",
    "After a price spike (≥ 70.00), model often overshoots in the next 3-5 days; apply a downward correction of 3-8% to prevent overreaction.",
    "Model consistently underestimates prices when recent history shows a downward trend (e.g., 3 consecutive negative sentiment or falling prices); adjust forecast upward by 2-5% to reflect mean reversion.",
    "If model forecast is below 60.00 and true outcome is above 62.00, consider a bias correction: add 2-5% to forecast to account for market rebound.",
    "For horizon > 15 days, model tends to underestimate true price; apply a 3-7% upward bias to align with longer-term mean reversion patterns.",
    "When sentiment history includes a negative sentiment (≤ -0.25), model often underestimates prices; adjust forecast upward by 3-7% to reflect risk aversion or market correction."
  ]
}
